Title: Telecommunications | Colliers Engineering & Design
Content: ## Telecommunications

Colliers Engineering & Design's Telecommunications group delivers full-service engineering for fiber optic networks, wireless infrastructure, and broadband deployment. Our team of engineers, GIS specialists, and project managers brings deep expertise in outside plant (OSP) design, permitting, and construction management.

**Service Areas:**
- **Fiber Optic Network Design** — Route analysis, network architecture, splice planning, and construction drawing production
- **GIS Mapping & Analysis** — Spatial data collection, management, and integration with engineering workflows
- **Permitting** — Preparation and coordination of permit packages for municipal, county, state, and utility right-of-way applications
- **Make-Ready Engineering** — Aerial and underground assessment and engineering for pole attachments and conduit systems
- **Construction Management** — Field inspection, quality control, and construction oversight
- **BEAD Program Support** — Engineering, GIS, and documentation services for BEAD-funded network deployments

**Our Team**
Our telecommunications professionals operate from offices across the eastern United States, with project experience spanning rural broadband, municipal fiber networks, and large-scale ISP deployments.

**Technology Platform**
We integrate Esri ArcGIS with CAD tools including AutoCAD and MicroStation to produce accurate, permit-ready engineering deliverables. Our team is experienced with OSP network design platforms including Katapult Pro and IQGeo.

**Industries Served**
- Internet Service Providers (ISPs)
- Municipal and county governments
- Electric cooperatives
- Utilities and telecommunications carriers

</tool_response>

